<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Cengis K	   unloading   corn screening  5,999     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten feed     2,000</p>
<p>First Lady	 unloading   soya	     16,384     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   2,871</p>
<p>				     wheat	     6,277</p>
<p>Marny		unloading   fishmeal	  8,335     Peru</p>
<p>Zanet 2	    in port     rye		 3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobalt 186    in port     wheat	     2,700     Europe</p>
<p>Malanga	    in port     rapeseed meal   3,299     n/a</p>
<p>Peleduy	   18/6	   wheat	     2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Flag Leader     18/6	   barley	   30,500     U.S.</p>
<p>Liberty Spirit  21/6	   soya	     43,691     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn	     15,820</p>
<p>Geroy Arsenela  21/6	   maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Aspilos	   24/6	   sorghum	  22,770     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn screening  6,018</p>
<p>				     corn gluten     2,855</p>
<p>Bodaybo	   24/6	   wheat	     2,700     Europe</p>
<p>Flag Nicolas    10/7	   corn	     21,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	    9,000</p>
<p>Matheus	   10/7	   TBN		60,000     U.S.</p>
